A loan was repaid in two annual instatements of Rs. 121/- each. If the rate of interest be 10% per annum compounded annually, the sum borrowed was
Rs.120
Rs.220
Rs.201
Rs.210
Solution:
Working: The sum borrowed is the present value of both installments.
Sum = 121/(1.1) + 121/(1.1)²
= 110 + 100
= Rs. 210
Check:
Year 1: 210 × 1.1 = 231. After paying 121, the balance is 110.
Year 2: 110 × 1.1 = 121. After paying 121, the balance is 0 ✓
Answer: 210
